==Trivia==
*Aside from succession via Might makes right, Septimont's system of government somewhat resembles that of ancient Sparta, with the Ephor and Priestess of Septimont advised by a Council of Elders bearing similarities to the List of kings of Sparta who are in turn advised, ironically, by five individuals holding the title of Ephor, though the Elders are more akin to the Gerousia. Though, unlike the Spartan Ephors and Gerousia, the Septimont Council of Elders have no judicial authority over the Ephor and Priestess.
===Etymology===
*Septimont is derived from Latin ''septem montes'', meaning “seven mountains” or “seven hills.” The name references Rome, traditionally known as the city of the Seven Hills.

